Samira Khan: quick FYI i'm opening a docs PR to rename the ingestion field `metering.event` -> `usage.event` across quickstarts, SDK examples, and the tier mapping page. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/914 (internal)

Derek Lowe: is this backwards compatible? any server-side aliasing?

Samira Khan: yes, server will accept `metering.event` as an alias for 21 days. docs will show both fields with a deprecation banner and a short migration snippet. added checklist in PR.

Vikram Patel: can you include a Rust SDK snippet? we haven't had a canonical Rust example in these pages and some customers asked for it.

Samira Khan: added a minimal Rust example to the PR:

```
// rust reqwest example
use reqwest::blocking::Client;
use std::env;

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
  let key = env::var("RW_KEY")?;
  let client = Client::new();
  let json = serde_json::json!({
    "tenant_id": "acme",
    "usage": { "event": "chat_completion", "units": 250 }
  });
  let resp = client.post("https://api.redwood.ai/v1/usage/report")
    .bearer_auth(key)
    .json(&json)
    .send()?;
  println!("{}", resp.status());
  Ok(())
}
```

Samira Khan: note the payload uses `usage.event` in the new examples; we also show the old `metering.event` variant in a small compatibility table.

Derek Lowe: nice. can you paste the small curl + PromQL examples you added? i'll use them in the ops playbook.

Samira Khan: curl:

```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/usage/report \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $RW_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"tenant_id":"acme","usage":{"event":"chat_completion","units":250}}'
```

PromQL (shows both fields during transition):

```
sum by (tenant) (increase(redwood_metered_tokens_total{event=~"(metering.event|usage.event)"}[30d]))
```

Vikram Patel: for alerts i'd prefer warning at 75% committed and critical at 95%. include both avg/max variants in docs so users can pick.

Samira Khan: added alert snippets and a short FAQ about burst accounts (different thresholds). also added a staging preview link in the PR.

